# Select Label Rule

**Rule:** `<Select>` components that are pre-filled from DB data (UUIDs, slugs, IDs) MUST explicitly pass the resolved label as children of `<SelectValue>`. Never rely solely on shadcn's auto-lookup — it fails when the options list loads asynchronously after the value is set.

## Pattern

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — shows UUID if options haven't loaded yet
<Select value={roleId}>
  <SelectTrigger>
    <SelectValue placeholder="Select role…" />
  </SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>
    {roles.map((r) => (
      <SelectItem key={r.id} value={r.id}>{r.display_name}</SelectItem>
    ))}
  </SelectContent>
</Select>

// ✅ GOOD — always shows the resolved label
<Select value={roleId}>
  <SelectTrigger>
    <SelectValue placeholder="Select role…">
      {roles.find((r) => r.id === roleId)?.display_name ?? "Select role…"}
    </SelectValue>
  </SelectTrigger>
  <SelectContent>
    {roles.map((r) => (
      <SelectItem key={r.id} value={r.id}>{r.display_name}</SelectItem>
    ))}
  </SelectContent>
</Select>
```

## When this matters

- Any `<Select>` pre-seeded with a value from DB (UUID foreign keys, slug strings, enum codes)
- Any `<Select>` whose options list is fetched asynchronously (common: roles, categories, lookup values)
- Edit forms / modals that open with existing data

## Rule

Always do `options.find(o => o.id === value)?.label ?? placeholder` as children of `<SelectValue>`.
